<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's TBC rate said cut to 1.62 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Brazil's TBC rate said cut to 1.62 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank has cut its March Basic Interest Rate (TBC) for operations in the financial markets to 1.62 percent, Gazeta Mercantil newspaper said.</p>
<p>The TBC, which is set on a monthly basis and was first introduced in July, is used as a reference rate for Central Bank rediscount lines and Proer credit lines.</p>
<p>February's TBC rate was set at 1.66 percent.</p>
<p>The Central Bank's Financian Assistance Rate (TBAN) was cut to 1.80 percent for March, from 1.84 percent in February, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Rio de Janeiro newsroom 5521 507 4151))</p>
